4. Techniques and texts credited where they are used (no code copied):
   - the int4-to-fp16 dequantization by magic numbers and LOP3 (kernels/formats.cuh,
     cuda/int4_gemm.cu) follows Marlin (https://github.com/IST-DASLab/marlin, Apache-2.0) and
     FasterTransformer (https://github.com/NVIDIA/FasterTransformer, Apache-2.0);
   - the Kimi Delta Attention step order and its chunked form (crates/fullm/src/ops.rs,
     kernels/kda_chunk.cuh) follow flash-linear-attention
     (https://github.com/fla-org/flash-linear-attention, MIT) and the gated delta rule
     (Yang, Kautz and Hatamizadeh, "Gated Delta Networks", 2024);
   - the Kimi tokenizer's split pattern (KIMI_PATTERN in crates/fullm/src/tokenizer.rs) is
     Moonshot AI's, from tokenization_kimi.py of the Kimi models;
   - the tool-calling preamble of Qwen3's chat template (crates/fullm/src/tokenizer.rs) is
     Qwen's text (https://huggingface.co/Qwen, Apache-2.0);
   - the tiny Kimi K3 test checkpoint (tests/fixtures/tiny_k3) was generated with
     make_tiny_checkpoint.py of https://github.com/FareedKhan-dev/kimi-k3-in-c (Apache-2.0).
